# Local EIS Viewer — your paths.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder as run_dashboard.py) and edit it.
# This is THE ONE PLACE a path is ever written down. No Python file in this
# project contains a personal path, and none needs editing to point the viewer
# at different data.
#
# Rules:
#   * Windows paths are written as they appear in Explorer. No quotes needed,
#     no doubled backslashes, spaces are fine:
#         EIS_FAMOS_ROOT=C:\Users\me\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis
#   * Lines starting with # are ignored.
#   * A command-line flag beats this file, so `--famos D:\other` is a one-off
#     override that does not mean editing anything here.
#   * Several folders at once: separate with ";" on Windows, ":" on Linux/macOS.
#
# Restart the app after changing this file.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. RAW FAMOS RECORDINGS  (.DAT)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The folder holding the .DAT files. Subfolders are searched too, so this can
# point at the campaign folder or at its parent.
EIS_FAMOS_ROOT=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis
# A network share works too, written exactly as Explorer shows it:
# EIS_FAMOS_ROOT=\\bosch.com\DfsRB\DfsDE\LOC\Fe\ILM\A_ILM_DSETD\Gruppenablage\EAT3\Charan\Lokale_EIS\Daten\2611976_16_07
# but process it with `run_evaluation.py --stage-local`: the reader memory-maps
# each card and bronze walks it repeatedly, so over SMB every page fault is a
# network round trip. Where the local copies go:
# EIS_STAGE_DIR=C:\Users\uum5fe\eis_stage

# Filename pattern, if a campaign names its files differently. Two conventions
# are recognised out of the box and need no setting here:
#     Leepa_<order>_Current_<condition>_Test_<nn>_Karte_<n>.DAT
#     RO<order>-01_Current_<condition>_Test_<nn>_Karte_<n>.DAT
# For anything else, give a regex with named groups measurement_id, condition,
# test and card:
# EIS_FAMOS_REGEX=Cell(?P<measurement_id>\d+)_(?P<condition>\d+A)_(?P<test>\d+)_(?P<card>\d+)\.DAT$


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1b. RAW R2-D2 CSV SWEEPS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The folder holding the sweep folders. One sweep = one folder containing
# metadata.csv plus p1.csv, p2.csv, ... (one file per frequency). Point this at
# the PARENT of those folders -- subfolders are searched:
#
#     csv_files\<sweep folder>\metadata.csv
#     csv_files\<sweep folder>\p1.csv, p2.csv, ...
#
# This is what the Gen 2 plate is measured with; there is no FAMOS recording
# for Gen 2. Leave it unset and only the FAMOS and results roots are searched,
# which is why a sweep kept in its own folder is not found until this is set.
EIS_CSV_ROOT=\\bosch.com\DfsRB\DfsDE\LOC\Fe\ILM\A_ILM_DSETD\Gruppenablage\EAT3\Charan\Lokale_EIS\csv_files


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. PROCESSED RESULTS  (CSV / Parquet)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where finished pipeline output lives, laid out as
#     <root>\<order id>\<condition>\gold\plate_summary.csv
#     <root>\<order id>\<condition>\silver\spectra_clean.csv
# e.g. C:\Users\uum5fe\Local_Eis_results\2611976\45A\gold\...
EIS_RESULTS_ROOT=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis\results


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. PROCESSING RAW .DAT  (not needed if you only view finished results)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bronze/silver/gold pipeline is bundled in local_eis/ — the same modules
# that ran on Databricks. Point this somewhere else only if you keep your own
# copy of it.
# EIS_PIPELINE_DIR=C:\Users\uum5fe\Local_EIS_fixed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. CALIBRATION  (only needed to PROCESS raw .DAT, not to view results)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The per-segment shunt calibration is the only absolute scale in the chain
# once the potentiostat is gone. Without it, impedances come out in shunt volts
# per amp rather than in ohms.
# EIS_CURR_CAL=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis\cal\curr.csv
# EIS_TEMP_CAL=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis\cal\temp.csv
# Optional per-segment area override CSV.
# EIS_AREAS_FILE=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis\cal\areas.csv

# Let the app run the pipeline itself on raw .DAT. Fine on a laptop with the
# files local; leave off on a shared server.
# EIS_ALLOW_INLINE_PIPELINE=1

# Results are written straight into EIS_RESULTS_ROOT above, so a finished run
# is immediately visible in the dashboard. This is only the fallback for when
# EIS_RESULTS_ROOT is unset.
# EIS_SCRATCH_RESULTS=C:\Users\uum5fe\Local_Eis_results


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CALIBRATION CAMPAIGNS ("Abgleichdaten")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folders of Step<n>_<T>Grad.csv plus coefficients/. A campaign belongs to a
# plate, not to a measurement order, so it is picked by folder name and no
# order id is asked for. Leave this unset and the roots above are searched too.
# EIS_CALIBRATION_ROOT=C:\Users\uum5fe\Lokale_EIS\Abgleichdaten


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. PLATE GENERATIONS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extra folder of plate spec JSON files, so a Gen 2 plate can be added without
# touching the repository.
# EIS_PLATE_SPEC_DIR=C:\Users\uum5fe\OneDrive - Bosch Group\Local_Eis\plate_specs
# Two are bundled: gen1_r2d2_72 (green/Kashyyyk) and gen2_r2d2_naboo_72
# (blue/Naboo). Both are verified: 72 segments tiling the 45x20 pad grid
# exactly once, 304.92 cm2 in total. Set this to gen2_r2d2_naboo_72 if the
# plate you usually work on is the Gen 2 one.
EIS_DEFAULT_PLATE=gen1_r2d2_72


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. APP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EIS_TITLE=Local EIS Viewer
# PORT=8050


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. DATABRICKS  (leave unset when running on your own machine)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EIS_DATAGO_METADATA_TABLE=<catalog>.<schema>.datago_advtec_metadata
# EIS_DATAGO_PROPERTIES_TABLE=<catalog>.<schema>.datago_advtec_generalproperties
# DATABRICKS_HOST=https://<workspace>.cloud.databricks.com
# DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID=<warehouse id>
